      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Greg,\n\nXR21V141X cannot use normal usb acm driver and has its owner driver.\nIf CONFIG_USB_SERIAL_XR was not enabled in gki_defconfig,\nthe XR21V141X device will be configured as a cdc_acm device (ttyACM0), which is not working. (XR21V141X uses ttyXRUSB0.)\n\nPlease refer to https://www.spinics.net/lists/linux-usb/msg195926.html\n\n\"The RTS/CTS line discipline for this device doesn\u0027t follow\nthe standard. So, in order to properly support TX, a separate\ndriver is needed.\n\nEnsure that cdc_acm will ignore it during probe time, if the\nKernel is built with support for it.\"\n\nThanks.",
      "parentUuid": "ef1fe26a_0e628432",
